Third-party parts
-----------------
- Polyfrost OneLauncher (GPL-3.0-only): parts of the launcher's process handling are adapted from
  https://github.com/Polyfrost/OneLauncher
- Chat Heads by dzwdz (MPL-2.0): parts of the TRS Client chat heads code (client-mod, packages
  "chatheads") are based on https://github.com/dzwdz/chat_heads. Those files keep their MPL-2.0
  header; the license text is in client-mod/licenses/chat-heads-MPL-2.0.txt.
- AppleSkin by squeek502 (The Unlicense): idea for the TRS Client hunger overlay; resource packs
  that ship AppleSkin textures are supported.
- Amethyst-iOS by Tran Hoang Khanh Duy and the PojavLauncher/Amethyst contributors (GPL-3.0):
  the iOS game engine (JVM start, GL/EGL and input bridge, JIT detection and dyld helpers) is based
  on https://github.com/AngelAuraMC/Amethyst-iOS at commit 9212a1894865e7ac0466029e25ddb0d895544c76.
  Vendored files, local patches and the parts taken at build time are listed in
  src-tauri/plugins/tauri-plugin-trs-game/ios/Engine/vendor/amethyst-ios/UPSTREAM.md. The iOS app
  additionally ships, unchanged from that commit: MobileGlues (LGPL-2.1), ANGLE (BSD-3-Clause),
  gl4es (MIT), Mesa OSMesa (MIT), MoltenVK (Apache-2.0), LWJGL (BSD-3-Clause), OpenAL Soft
  (LGPL-2.0), FreeType (FTL), shaderc (Apache-2.0), Caciocavallo (GPL-2.0 with Classpath
  Exception), fishhook (BSD-3-Clause), Gson (Apache-2.0). Java runtimes (OpenJDK, GPL-2.0 with
  Classpath Exception) are downloaded by the app at runtime and are not part of it.
- Further libraries and bundled mods are listed with their licenses in README.md and
